From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: streamed signed and enveloped messages, BER content in the message decoder (3757)

A signed message opened with a CMSG_STREAM_INFO sent only part of its output
(the signed content went through the hash and the callback never saw a byte),
and an enveloped one sent nothing at all. Both now stream BER with indefinite
lengths to the callback: the header at the first update, the content in chunks,
and the closing octets with the certificates and signer infos (signed) or the
last cipher blocks (enveloped) in the final call. CMSG_BARE_CONTENT_FLAG
leaves out the outer content info, CMSG_DETACHED_FLAG the content. The message
decoder now reads such BER (indefinite lengths, constructed strings) by turning
it into DER first. CORE review: security (patches/notes/3757.txt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS
---
diff --git a/dlls/crypt32/msg.c b/dlls/crypt32/msg.c
index 40451a9..7bb0f0a 100644
--- a/dlls/crypt32/msg.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/msg.c
@@ -113,6 +113,314 @@ static inline void CryptMsgBase_Init(CryptMsgBase *msg, DWORD dwFlags,
     msg->state = MsgStateInit;
